{\pard\sb0\sa80 \qc\b\fs48\cf1 VibeFinder Song Guide\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \qc\i\fs20\cf3 An in-depth knowledge document for retrieval-augmented music recommendations\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \qc\i\fs20\cf3 20 songs - 20 genre notes - 9 activity guides\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa80 \b\fs32\cf1 About this document\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \fs20 This guide describes every song in the VibeFinder catalog (data/songs.csv) in depth: its sound, vocals, structure, lyric themes, when to play it and when to skip it, how it compares with similar songs, and direct answers to common questions. All songs and artists are fictional and were created for a classroom project. Feature values come directly from the catalog; activity playlists were produced by running the VibeFinder recommender itself, so this guide never contradicts the app.\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \fs20 How VibeFinder uses it: the retriever extracts the text and splits it into one chunk per song, from the line 'Song: <title>' to the line 'End of song: <title>'. When a request names a song ('songs like Storm Runner'), the agent copies that song's genre, mood and energy. When a request names a sound ('piano', 'fiddle', 'no vocals'), songs whose Sound or Vocals lines mention it get a bonus, and the matching sections are passed to the language model as evidence.\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \fs20 Contents: 1. Catalog at a glance - 2. Songs in depth - 3. Activity playlists - 4. Genre guide - 5. Mood map - 6. Glossary\par}
