{\pard\sb240\sa80 \b\fs32\cf1 Chapter 6: Glossary\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \fs18 {\b Energy:} How intense and active a song feels, from 0.0 (very calm) to 1.0 (very intense). VibeFinder rewards closeness to the energy you want, not 'higher is better'.\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \fs18 {\b Valence:} How positive a song sounds, from 0.0 (sad, dark) to 1.0 (happy, bright).\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \fs18 {\b Danceability:} How suitable the rhythm is for dancing, from 0.0 to 1.0.\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \fs18 {\b Acousticness:} How acoustic (real instruments, unplugged) versus electronic or produced a song sounds, from 0.0 to 1.0.\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \fs18 {\b Tempo (BPM):} Beats per minute. Around 60-80 BPM feels slow, 90-120 moderate, 125+ fast.\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \fs18 {\b Instrumental:} A song with no sung or rapped vocals. Marked in this guide as 'Vocals: none (instrumental)'.\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \fs18 {\b Related genre:} A genre that fans of another genre usually also enjoy, taken from the VibeFinder genre notes. Related genres earn half of the genre points when ranking.\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \fs18 {\b Mood family:} Groups of moods that feel alike: chill/relaxed/focused, happy/euphoric/confident, intense/angry, and sad/melancholy/moody/nostalgic.\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa80 \fs18 {\b Confidence:} VibeFinder's own estimate of how well it understood and matched a request (0 to 1). Below 0.5 it asks the listener for more detail.\par}
